# AC196: given lyceum/spec/brief.md, then it defines no AC whatever it quotes, and the project gate is pending, and approve project goes ahead, only when the registry lists an area other than brief
# The brief is the owner's words kept verbatim: a quoted AC row or bullet in it is not a definition.
# ttyrun runs the command on a pty, so stdin and stdout are both a terminal.
cd $REPO

exec lyceum init
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m 'lyceum init'

# The interview saved a brief that quotes an AC row and an AC bullet; only brief is registered.
cp $WORK/brief-only.md lyceum/SPEC.md
mkdir lyceum/spec
cp $WORK/brief.md lyceum/spec/brief.md
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m 'brief'

# With only brief registered, project is not pending and approving it refuses.
exec lyceum status
stdout '^Pending approvals: none$'
cp lyceum/events.jsonl $WORK/events-before.jsonl
ttyrun $WORK/project.txt 'lyceum approve project'
stdout '^exit=2$'
stderr '^Can''t approve project: no area other than brief is registered in the area registry of lyceum/SPEC.md, so there is nothing to approve$'
! stderr 'Type the gate name'
cmp lyceum/events.jsonl $WORK/events-before.jsonl

# The quoted AC1 and AC2 define nothing: no registry finding, no unclaimed AC.
exec sh -c 'lyceum check --ci; echo "exit=$?"'
stdout '^exit=0$'
! stdout 'registry'
! stdout 'AC1'
! stdout 'AC2'

# Once another area is registered, project is pending.
cp $WORK/spec-index.md lyceum/SPEC.md
cp $WORK/orders.md lyceum/spec/orders.md
exec lyceum status
stdout '^  project for lyceum/SPEC.md: run "lyceum approve project" yourself in a terminal$'
exec sh -c 'lyceum check --ci; echo "exit=$?"'
! stdout 'registry'

-- project.txt --
project
-- brief-only.md --
# Specification index

This file is the index. Load an area file only when the work needs it.

## Area registry

The CLI owns this table.

| Area | File | Covers | ACs |
|---|---|---|---|
| brief | `spec/brief.md` | The owner's brief, verbatim | |
-- spec-index.md --
# Specification index

This file is the index. Load an area file only when the work needs it.

## Area registry

The CLI owns this table.

| Area | File | Covers | ACs |
|---|---|---|---|
| brief | `spec/brief.md` | The owner's brief, verbatim | |
| orders | `spec/orders.md` | Orders and their lifecycle | AC3 |
-- brief.md --
# Brief

A shop that takes orders. Like the old one:

| AC1 | Given an order, when it is placed, then it is saved |

- **AC2** Given a saved order, when it ships, then it is marked shipped
-- orders.md --
# Orders

| AC3 | Given an order, when it is placed, then it is saved |
